# The root lockfile is package-lock.json — yarn is not used here (dropped from
# mise.toml in ede9e6974; CI and CLAUDE.md both use npm/bun). EAS picks its
# package manager from whichever lockfile is present, so keeping a stray
# yarn.lock made EAS build with yarn while everything else used npm.
#
# package-lock.json is not caught by ~/.gitignore_global's "*.lock" rule, so it
# needs no negation. The old "!yarn.lock" line existed only to defeat that rule.

# Self-hosted runner installs. A GitHub Actions runner was once unpacked into
# this repo root, and its scripts were committed alongside a 68 MB CircleCI
# runner binary. circleci-runner and swiftly.pkg were already listed above but
# stayed tracked, because .gitignore does not untrack files already in the
# index. They are untracked now; these rules stop them coming back.
actions-runner/
/config.sh
/run.sh
/run
/run-helper.sh
/run-helper.sh.template
/run-helper.cmd.template

# Shell redirect accidents and editor leftovers committed at the repo root.
